course: dictionary
lesson: 15949
title: Unspecified: not said clearly
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: When something is unspecified, it has not been stated clearly or exactly. Look at its parts: un- means not, and specify means to name something clearly. «The party will start at an unspecified time.» We know there is a time, but nobody has said exactly what it is.
explain: Check your meaning with the swap test. Put «not stated clearly» into the sentence: «The party will start at a time nobody has said clearly.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Clue words like «an» with no exact number, or «some», often show that something is unspecified.
explain: In maths word problems, «an unspecified number» is a number that is not given. You may need to find it from clues, or call it a letter like n. «Find the unspecified number n when n + 4 = 10.» Here n is 6. In everyday life, «for an unspecified reason» means the reason was not said.
fact: Unspecified means not stated clearly or exactly.
fact: Un- means not, and specify means to name something clearly, so unspecified means not named clearly.
fact: «An unspecified number» means a number that is not given, so you may need to find it or call it a letter like n.
fact: «For an unspecified reason» means the reason was not said.
fact: Unspecified is a formal word, often found in exams, legal documents and news reports.
exercise: «The shop will open on an unspecified day next week.» What does unspecified mean here? | *Not stated clearly | Closed forever | Very small | Open every day
exercise: «Find the unspecified number n when n + 4 = 10.» What is n? | 14 | *6 | 10 | 4
exercise: «The letter was sent for an unspecified reason.» Which is true? | *The reason was not said | Everyone knows the reason | The reason was written in big letters | The letter was sent by a king
test: Which word is closest in meaning to unspecified? | Heavy | *Vague | Loud | Quick
test: «The meeting will happen at an unspecified time.» Why would a text use unspecified? | Because it is always lunchtime | *Because the time was not said clearly | Because there is no meeting at all | Because the time is written in clear numbers
exam: «Mum said she would call at an unspecified hour.» What is the best meaning of unspecified? | Exactly on the hour | Very early in the morning | *Not stated clearly | Done with great care
